  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "A flying sword rat wound on Hei Lou Lan is filled with dao marks of metal path. Those marks repel the strength path dao marks of her immortal body and resist the Great Strength True Martial Physique’s recovery, so even an extreme immortal body heals the cut only slowly.",
      "chapters": [
        716
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_hei_lou_lan",
        "sys_great_strength_true_martial_physique"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "General dao marks and attainment levels are covered on dao marks and attainment.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_dao_marks"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "When Shi Lei fights as an iron crown eagle, the star demon bat’s body fills with injuries that all carry metal path dao marks and cannot heal any time soon.",
      "chapters": [
        717
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "injuries-that-will-not-heal",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_shi_lei"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Later, accumulated flying sword rat damage leaves his own back injury filled with metal path dao marks, turning small cuts into a large wound.",
      "chapters": [
        727
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "injuries-that-will-not-heal",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cicada-like wings show the light of dao marks of metal path. Only a quasi-rank nine dao mark foundation makes that light visible to the naked eye.",
      "chapters": [
        935
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "visible-light-on-bee-wings",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "A tiger-striped honey bee wing mainly contains metal path dao marks and is useful for refining a metal path Immortal Gu, but useless for star thought Immortal Gu.",
      "chapters": [
        936
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "visible-light-on-bee-wings",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_immortal_gu",
        "gu_star_thought_immortal_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Lang Ya land spirit confirms the metal path dao marks on such a wing are dense enough that the light can be seen with the naked eye.",
      "chapters": [
        975
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "visible-light-on-bee-wings",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_lang_ya_land_spirit"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Qin Ding Ling abandoned metal path to cultivate luck path after Giant Sun Immortal Venerable died. She abandoned all of her metal path dao marks and turned them into a metal coffin, then hibernated deep in an earth vein with Heavenly Court help to comprehend luck path.",
      "chapters": [
        1821
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "abandoned-into-a-metal-coffin",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_qin_ding_ling",
        "char_giant_sun_immortal_venerable",
        "fac_heavenly_court"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "If an immortal aperture gains metal path dao marks, a large amount of ores appear in the soil and soil fertility changes, affecting vegetation above.",
      "chapters": [
        2109
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "ores-and-disaster-resonance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "When meteor rain enters Mini Yellow Heaven, it resonates with metal path dao marks and its might increases to rank eight.",
      "chapters": [
        2127
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
